                {
                  "type": "application",
                  "title": "Case 4 — Two Separate Code Sets (Mother + Newborn)",
                  "content": "**Critical rule:** Maternal chart uses **Chapter 15 (O codes)** only. Newborn chart uses **Chapter 16 (P codes)** only. They are **two distinct records**, two distinct code sets, two distinct DRGs.\n\n**MOTHER — ICD-10-CM:**\n1. **O14.13** — Severe pre-eclampsia, third trimester (PDX — reason for admission/delivery)\n2. **O60.14X0** — Preterm labor third trimester w preterm delivery third trimester, single gestation (the 7th character 0 = single fetus / not applicable)\n3. **O09.513** — Supervision of elderly primigravida — NOT here, patient is multipara, so skip\n4. **Z3A.34** — 34 weeks gestation\n5. **Z37.0** — Single live birth (ALWAYS on maternal delivery record)\n\n**MOTHER — ICD-10-PCS:**\n- **10D00Z1** — Extraction of products of conception, low cervical, open approach (the C-section: section 1 Obstetrics, root Extraction D, body part 0 POC, approach 0 open, device Z, qualifier 1 low cervical)\n- **3E0234Z** — Introduction of serum/toxoid/vaccine into muscle, percutaneous (betamethasone IM — institutional decision whether to code)\n\n**NEWBORN — ICD-10-CM:**\n1. **P22.0** — Respiratory distress syndrome of newborn (PDX — primary reason for newborn admission/care)\n2. **P07.37** — Preterm newborn, 34 completed weeks\n3. **P07.17** — Other low birth weight newborn, 2000-2249 g\n4. **Z38.01** — Single liveborn infant, delivered by cesarean (PDX-equivalent on day of birth admission — coded FIRST on birth record per I.C.16.a)\n\n**Important:** On newborn admission for birth, **Z38.0-** is sequenced FIRST. If RDS were the only reason for a TRANSFER admission later, P22.0 would be principal. Read admission context carefully.\n\n**NEWBORN — ICD-10-PCS:**\n- **5A1935Z** — Respiratory ventilation, less than 24 consecutive hours (BUT 36 hours = 24-96 hr range = **5A1945Z**)\n- **3E0F7GC** — Introduction of other therapeutic substance into respiratory tract, via natural opening (surfactant)\n- **0BH17EZ** — Insertion of endotracheal airway, via natural opening (intubation)",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">CASE 4: TWO CODE SETS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Maternal chart vs newborn chart — never mix</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"500\" height=\"780\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(236,72,153,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ec4899\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">MOTHER (O + Z codes)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">CM Diagnoses:</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PDX O14.13</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Severe pre-eclampsia, 3rd tri</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX O60.14X0</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"440\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Preterm labor w preterm del</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX Z3A.34   34 weeks</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"525\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX Z37.0      Single liveborn</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"585\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PCS Procedures:</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"625\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">10D00Z1</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Extraction POC, low cervical,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"690\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">open (the C-section)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DRG 766 / 767</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">(Cesarean w/wo CC/MCC)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Z37 = ALWAYS on</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ec4899\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">maternal delivery record</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"190\" width=\"480\" height=\"780\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">NEWBORN (P + Z codes)</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"300\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">CM Diagnoses:</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"335\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PDX Z38.01 (birth)</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"365\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Liveborn, cesarean</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"410\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX P22.0     RDS</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"450\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX P07.37  Preterm 34 wk</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"490\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX P07.17  LBW 2000-2249g</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"555\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PCS Procedures:</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"595\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">5A1945Z   Vent 24-96 hr</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"635\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">0BH17EZ   Insert ET tube</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"675\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">3E0F7GC   Surfactant</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">DRG 791 / 793 (newborn</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"790\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">w major problem)</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">P-codes ONLY on</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">newborn record</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Case 4 split: maternal O-codes vs newborn P-codes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "On the newborn record for the infant in Case 4, the coder is unsure whether to sequence Z38.01 or P22.0 first. Which rule applies to the BIRTH ADMISSION?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "P22.0 is sequenced first because it is the most clinically significant condition.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Z38.01 is sequenced first per Guideline I.C.16.a — the appropriate code from category Z38 (Liveborn infants according to place of birth and type of delivery) is the principal diagnosis for the birth episode, with all other conditions assigned as additional codes.",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Whichever code carries the higher MS-DRG weight should be sequenced first.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "P07.37 (preterm) is sequenced first because gestational age affects all other conditions.",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "Guideline **I.C.16.a.1** is explicit: 'When coding the birth episode in a newborn record, assign a code from category Z38 as the principal diagnosis.' Z38.01 (single liveborn, cesarean) is the PDX on the birth admission. P22.0, P07.37, P07.17, and any other newborn conditions are secondary diagnoses. The Z38 code is used **only once** — on the birth admission record, never on subsequent admissions.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Newborn birth admission sequencing</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"1000\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">BIRTH ADMISSION (Z38)</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PDX  Z38.01    Single liveborn, cesarean</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  P22.0      RDS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  P07.37    Preterm 34 weeks</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  P07.17    LBW 2000-2249 g</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"480\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Guideline I.C.16.a.1 — ALWAYS Z38 first</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"540\" width=\"1000\" height=\"320\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"600\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">SUBSEQUENT ADMISSION</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">If baby is later RE-admitted for RDS treatment:</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"705\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PDX  P22.0      RDS</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">No Z38 — used only ONCE on birth episode.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Z38 lives on the birth record forever.</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"900\" width=\"900\" height=\"160\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"955\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Maternal record never carries P-codes.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"995\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Newborn record never carries O-codes.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1035\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Two charts. Two distinct code worlds.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Newborn birth admission sequencing rule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "example",
                  "title": "Case 5 — MVA Polytrauma: Splenectomy + ORIF",
                  "content": "**Patient:** 27-year-old male, **unrestrained driver** in single-vehicle MVA, struck tree at ~50 mph. Brought by EMS.\n\n**Trauma bay:** GCS 14. HR 138, BP 88/52, abdominal tenderness LUQ, decreased breath sounds left, deformed right thigh.\n\n**Imaging:** FAST positive (free fluid LUQ). CT: **grade IV splenic laceration with active extravasation**; **left tension pneumothorax** (chest tube placed in trauma bay); **comminuted right midshaft femoral shaft fracture**; **closed left distal radius fracture**.\n\n**Surgeries (HD#0):**\n*Operative report excerpt 1 — Exploratory laparotomy, splenectomy:*\n*'Midline laparotomy. ~1,500 mL hemoperitoneum evacuated. Spleen with grade IV laceration through hilum, ongoing bleeding. **Total splenectomy** performed by dividing splenic artery and vein, ligating short gastric vessels. Specimen sent to pathology. Hemostasis confirmed. Abdomen closed.'*\n\n*Operative report excerpt 2 — ORIF right femur:*\n*'Right lateral thigh approach. Fracture reduced under fluoroscopy. **Intramedullary rod placed antegrade from greater trochanter**, locked proximally and distally with screws. Reduction confirmed.'*\n\n*Operative report excerpt 3 — Closed reduction left distal radius with cast.*\n\n**Hospital course:** Chest tube to suction, removed HD#3. Vaccinations given post-splenectomy. D/C HD#6.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">CASE 5: MVA POLYTRAUMA</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">27M unrestrained driver, struck tree at 50 mph</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">INJURIES</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Grade IV splenic lac</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">  w/ active extravasation</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Left tension pneumothorax</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Comminuted R femoral</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">  shaft fracture</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"495\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Closed L distal radius fx</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Hemodynamically unstable</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"190\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">PROCEDURES</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">1. Chest tube (L)</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">2. Ex-lap +</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">    total splenectomy</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">3. ORIF R femur w/</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"455\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">    IM rod, screws</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"500\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">4. Closed reduction +</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"530\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">    cast L distal radius</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"600\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">SEQUENCING TASK</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Multiple injuries: code</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">each, sequence MOST</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SEVERE as principal.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Spleen w/ extravasation</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"885\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">= life-threatening =</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"925\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">principal candidate</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"600\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(20,184,166,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">EXTERNAL CAUSE</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">V47.5XXA</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Car driver vs fixed obj,</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"775\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">traffic, initial enc</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"820\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Y92.411 / Y93.C9</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"850\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">Place + activity</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"900\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">7th char A = initial</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">encounter all injuries</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Case 5 clinical summary"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "application",
                  "title": "Case 5 — Building the Code Set (Multi-Injury + Multi-Procedure)",
                  "content": "**Sequencing rule:** When multiple injuries are present, code **each separately** and sequence the **most severe** (the one that occasioned admission/required most resources) as principal. Here: the splenic laceration with active extravasation drove the emergent laparotomy — it is principal.\n\n**ICD-10-CM (sequenced):**\n1. **S36.032A** — Major laceration of spleen, initial encounter (PDX, MCC — grade IV captured as major)\n2. **S27.0XXA** — Traumatic pneumothorax, initial encounter\n3. **S72.351A** — Displaced comminuted fracture of shaft of right femur, initial encounter for closed fracture\n4. **S52.501A** — Unspecified fracture of lower end of left radius, initial encounter for closed fracture (use specific subtype if documented)\n5. **V47.5XXA** — Car driver injured in collision with fixed/stationary object in traffic accident, initial encounter\n6. **Y92.411** — Interstate highway as place of occurrence (or **Y92.488** if unknown specific road)\n7. **Y99.0** — Civilian activity done for income or pay — actually here Y99.8 (other external cause status) or unspecified\n8. **Z74.01** — Not applicable. Note: external cause codes are sequenced AFTER all injury codes.\n\n**ICD-10-PCS:**\n- **07TP0ZZ** — Resection of spleen, open approach (total splenectomy — root operation **Resection T** because entire body part removed)\n- **0WQB0ZZ** — NOT here. The chest tube: **0W9930Z** — Drainage of right pleural cavity, percutaneous, drainage device (left it in)\n- **0QS6X4Z** — Reposition of right upper femur with internal fixation, external approach? NO — **0QS604Z** — Reposition of right femoral shaft with internal fixation device, open approach (the IM rod via open lateral approach)\n- **0QSK0ZZ** — Reposition of left radius — NO, closed reduction = External approach. **0PSKXZZ** — Reposition of left radius, external approach\n- **2W3DXLZ** — Immobilization of left lower arm using cast (the cast)\n\n**CC/MCC:** S36.032A and S27.0XXA are MCCs. **MS-DRG 405-407** (Splenic procedures w MCC/CC/none) — splenectomy with MCC drives **MS-DRG 405**.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">CASE 5: CODE SET</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Multi-injury + multi-procedure inpatient stay</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"170\" width=\"1000\" height=\"360\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"220\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ICD-10-CM</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"270\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">PDX  S36.032A   Major laceration of spleen (MCC)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"310\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  S27.0XXA  Traumatic pneumothorax (MCC)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"350\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  S72.351A   Comminuted R femoral shaft fx</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"390\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  S52.501A   L distal radius fx, closed</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  V47.5XXA  Driver vs fixed object, traffic</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"470\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">SDX  Y92.411     Interstate highway location</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"560\" width=\"1000\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"610\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">ICD-10-PCS</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">07TP0ZZ     Resection of spleen, open</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"690\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">  Root T = entire body part removed</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"735\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">0W993ZZ    Drainage of R pleural cavity</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"765\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"18\">  Note: with drainage device left = 0W9930Z</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"810\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">0QS604Z   Reposition R femoral shaft, IM rod, open</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">0PSKXZZ   Reposition L radius, external (closed red.)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"895\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">2W3DXLZ  Immobilization L lower arm, cast</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"970\" width=\"900\" height=\"100\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"1015\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">MS-DRG 405 — Splenic procedure with MCC</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1050\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Spleen drives DRG; femur is a secondary procedure.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Case 5 final coded record"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "On Case 5, the splenectomy operative report describes 'total splenectomy.' A new coder selects root operation EXCISION (B). Why is this wrong?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "Excision is correct — any removal of an organ is Excision regardless of how much is removed.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The correct root operation is DETACHMENT (6) because the spleen is being separated from surrounding structures.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "The correct root operation is RESECTION (T) — Resection is defined as 'cutting out or off, without replacement, ALL of a body part.' Total splenectomy removes the entire body part 'spleen,' so Resection applies. Excision (B) would apply only to a partial splenectomy.",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Both Excision and Resection are required — code 07BP0ZZ first and 07TP0ZZ second.",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "The PCS distinction between **Excision (B)** and **Resection (T)** turns entirely on whether **all or a portion** of the body part is removed. Per ICD-10-PCS guideline B3.8: 'PCS contains specific body parts for anatomical subdivisions of a body part... Resection of the specific body part is coded whenever all of the body part is cut out or off.' The spleen has a single PCS body part value (P). A **total splenectomy removes all of body part 'spleen' → Resection (T)**. A partial splenectomy (e.g., wedge resection of one segment) would be **Excision (B)**.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Excision vs Resection — entire body part rule</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">EXCISION (B)</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cutting out or off,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">without replacement,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">a PORTION of a body part</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Examples:</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Liver biopsy</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"525\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Lumpectomy</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"190\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">RESECTION (T)</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Cutting out or off,</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">without replacement,</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">ALL of a body part</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Examples:</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Total splenectomy</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"525\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Appendectomy</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"600\" width=\"1000\" height=\"280\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">PCS GUIDELINE B3.8</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"710\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">&quot;Resection of the specific body part is coded</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"745\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">whenever ALL of the body part is cut out or off.&quot;</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"800\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Spleen = one body part value (P).</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"835\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Total splenectomy = Resection. End of story.</text><rect x=\"100\" y=\"920\" width=\"900\" height=\"140\" rx=\"35\" fill=\"rgba(255,215,0,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ffd700\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"975\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Trap: lobectomy of lung = Resection</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1015\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">(lung lobe is its own PCS body part).</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"1045\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"22\">Always check the PCS body part values.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Excision vs Resection — body part rule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "concept",
                  "title": "Synthesis: The Capstone Coding Mindset",
                  "content": "Five cases. Roughly **30 ICD-10-CM codes**, **12 ICD-10-PCS codes**, and **5 MS-DRGs** correctly assigned. What unifies them?\n\n**1. Read for the principal diagnosis.** The condition that **occasioned the admission** wins — not the most severe diagnosis, not the most chronic, not the most expensive. Read the H&P and discharge summary in tandem.\n\n**2. Sequencing rules trump intuition.** R65.21 cannot be principal even when shock is the most dramatic finding. Z38 leads on a newborn birth admission even when RDS demands all the attention. Memorize the explicit rules; do not invent them.\n\n**3. PCS is a building exercise.** Read the operative report. Identify the **body part actually acted on**, the **approach** the surgeon used, the **device** left at the end. Build the 7-character code character by character. Verify in the table.\n\n**4. Every CC and MCC is money.** R65.21, J96.01, S36.032A, S27.0XXA — these are not just diagnoses, they are the difference between MS-DRG 871 vs 872, between 405 vs 407. Capture every CC/MCC the documentation supports.\n\n**5. Two charts are two code sets.** Mother and newborn live in **separate chapters** of ICD-10-CM. Maternal record never sees a P-code; newborn record never sees an O-code.\n\n**6. When in doubt, query.** The compliant query (non-leading, options including 'unable to determine,' signed by physician) is the coder's most powerful compliance tool.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">THE CAPSTONE MINDSET</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">Six unifying principles across all five cases</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">1. PRINCIPAL DX</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">The condition that</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"340\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">OCCASIONED admission.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"395\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Not the most severe.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"430\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Not the most chronic.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">UHDDS, every time.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"190\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(139,92,246,0.15)\" stroke=\"#8b5cf6\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"245\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">2. SEQUENCING RULES</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">R65.2 NEVER principal.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Z38 always first on</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"380\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">  newborn birth chart.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"425\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Complication of chemo</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"460\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">  flips before Z51.11.</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"520\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#8b5cf6\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Memorize. Do not guess.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"600\" width=\"500\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(16,185,129,0.15)\" stroke=\"#10b981\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"300\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">3. PCS BUILD</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Body part acted on.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Approach surgeon used.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">Device left behind.</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"855\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">7 characters,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"890\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">one at a time,</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"925\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#10b981\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">verified in table.</text><rect x=\"570\" y=\"600\" width=\"480\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(245,158,11,0.15)\" stroke=\"#f59e0b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"810\" y=\"655\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">4-6. THE REST</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">4. Every CC/MCC = $$$</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"765\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">5. Two charts =</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">    two code sets</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"845\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">6. When in doubt,</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"880\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">    QUERY (compliant)</text><text x=\"610\" y=\"935\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#f59e0b\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Never assume. Never invent.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "The six principles that hold every case together"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "quiz",
                  "question": "Across all five cases in this lesson, which single coding principle most often determined whether the correct MS-DRG was assigned?",
                  "options": [
                    {
                      "text": "Selecting the most severe diagnosis as principal, regardless of admission reason.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Capturing every documented CC and MCC as secondary diagnoses, because a single MCC moves the DRG to the highest-paying tier (e.g., 871 vs 872, 405 vs 406 vs 407) and a single missed MCC can cost the facility thousands per admission.",
                      "correct": true
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Coding only the conditions treated during the admission, ignoring chronic conditions that did not require treatment.",
                      "correct": false
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Sequencing procedure codes in the order they were performed during the hospital stay.",
                      "correct": false
                    }
                  ],
                  "explanation": "Within most MS-DRG triplets (e.g., 870/871/872 for sepsis, 405/406/407 for splenectomy), the **presence or absence of a single MCC** shifts the case across tiers worth thousands of dollars. CCs and MCCs are listed in Appendix C of the **MS-DRG Definitions Manual**; coders must capture every one supported by documentation. Missing R65.21, J96.01, or even a documented acute blood-loss anemia can collapse a case from 'w MCC' to 'w/o CC/MCC' and trigger DRG validation denials.",
                  "visual": {
                    "type": "diagram",
                    "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 1100 1100\" class=\"lesson-visual\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"1100\" height=\"1100\" fill=\"#1a1a2e\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"70\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ffd700\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"36\">KNOWLEDGE CHECK</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"115\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#888\" font-size=\"24\">CC/MCC capture and MS-DRG impact</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"190\" width=\"1000\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(99,102,241,0.15)\" stroke=\"#6366f1\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"250\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">SEPSIS DRG TRIPLET</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"305\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">MS-DRG 870  Septicemia w/ MV &gt;96 hr</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"345\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">MS-DRG 871  Septicemia w/o MV &gt;96 hr w/ MCC</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"385\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">MS-DRG 872  Septicemia w/o MV &gt;96 hr w/o MCC</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"445\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">One MCC = the difference between</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"485\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">~$11K and ~$7K payment.</text><text x=\"550\" y=\"540\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#6366f1\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Every documented MCC counts.</text><rect x=\"50\" y=\"600\" width=\"1000\" height=\"380\" rx=\"20\" fill=\"rgba(239,68,68,0.15)\" stroke=\"#ef4444\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"550\" y=\"660\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"26\">COMMON MISSED MCCs</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"715\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">R65.21    Septic shock</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"755\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">J96.01    Acute resp failure w/ hypoxia</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"795\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">N17.9     Acute kidney failure</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"835\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">I21.4      NSTEMI</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"875\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"22\">D70.1     Chemo-induced agranulocytosis</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"925\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"#ef4444\" font-weight=\"bold\" font-size=\"22\">Read every progress note. Find them all.</text></svg>",
                    "caption": "Why MCC capture drives reimbursement"
                  }
                }
